  "notes": [
    "June 2026 signals are missing, so June 2026 CVEs use snapshot_month 2026-07: the 2026-07 scoreboard group holds June and July publications. 2026 per-month rates are grouped by snapshot_month.",
    "The 2026 scoreboard excludes CVEs already on KEV at their snapshot (built by the organisers with KEV data after 2025-12-31 that we do not have). The 2025 pool applies the same exclusion with our KEV file.",
    "assigner_no_prior_kev_share: share of rows whose assigner had 0 rows in known_exploited.csv with date_added before the first day of the row's snapshot month; every KEV row is mapped to its assigner via vulnerabilities.csv whatever the CVE's publish year (all 1,484 map). This is wider than the model's asg_kev feature, which counts only CVEs published 2021+.",
    "KEV additions during 2026 are not in our KEV file (it ends 2025-12-31), so the 2026 no-prior-KEV share is an upper bound: those additions could only lower it.",
    "cvss3 and product presence are today's NVD values: 2026 CVEs have had less time for NIST analysis (51,046 of 92,205 2026 CVEs unreviewed per README), so blank rates mix real drift with review backlog.",
    "epss_blank and any_public_exploit come from snapshot-month signals; Feb 2025 signals miss about 14,500 CVEs and EPSS changed model in March 2025, so 2025-02 and 2025-01 EPSS rates are not comparable to later months.",
    "monthly_volume.cves_published_per_month counts today's vulnerabilities.csv (rejected CVEs removed).",
    "GitHub advisories = assigner security-advisories@github.com only (product-cna@github.com is separate); VulnCheck = disclosure@vulncheck.com.",
    "No 2026 accuracy is claimed anywhere here: there are no 2026 labels."
  ]
}
